{"kind":"assert","text":"Adopt the complete C2 recovery successor revision 2 at dafb5b0c6e14f8959ad72f605fd50dee4039e0c7: main, corrections and full original acceptance map. I personally read all three current bodies (181528 UTF-8 bytes,2166 LF), recorded in76093f3c; freshly inspected all three effective nonstale artifact statements, complete live commission cf9050b4, delivery d6e25866 and full ordinary independent approval d268cae0. The builder accepted its own review; this act adopts the design and does not ratify that review again. All68 original conditions and both stages remain: authored45designed/20depends/3unresolved does not mean proved.\n\nThe attempt/instance/job/cut guards and unchanged journal-cut join repair the two prior P2 gaps within the existing save job and atomic guard table. Whole filesystem and Git closure, durable private journals, guarded verified checkpoint receipt/pointer, abrupt host loss, quiescence, uncertain side effects, exact unpushed commit, owned pins/expiry/deletion, former-holder privacy/export, real forks/tokens and the complete cross-device/review/publication journey are preserved. A new successful attempt does not settle an earlier unknown duty. Arbitrary command effects remain explicitly supervisor-trusted claims where no root-effect check is defined.\n\nPreserve all provider assumptions A1–A12 and RU-1–RU-20 and all source, authority, custody, cost and operational proof as owed. This is no provider verification, source acceptance, landing, deployment or real probe execution commission. Stage one requires a separate concrete commission naming provider/SDK/version, exact command, bounded resources/spend and meaningful recorded outcomes. Stage two still needs adopted relevant R1/R3 and independently reviewed I1/I3 and the real membership/hold/epoch/fork/token boundary. No storage double or prior pi experiment closes either real stage.\n\nExisting follow-through must reconcile the newly adopted R1/R2/R4 decisions and main1064–1066